      "identity_excerpt": "Revised April 2021 T H E M I S Y O U R IB A R O U N G L A W Y E R S S E C T I O N S MISSOURI SMALL CLAIMS COURT HANDBOOK Cases involving money in the amount of $5,000 or less I. Introduction to small claims court 1 II. Things to consider before bringing a claim 2 A. Who can I sue? What can I sue them for? B. When do I have to file my lawsuit? C. Can I settle before I sue? III. What should I do before I sue? 4 A. How do I prepare to bring my claim? 1. Get the correct name, address, and telephone number of the person or business being sued 2. How to determine type of business for purpose of naming defendant 3. Choose the right court (“venue”) 5 4. Filing for minors (under age 18) 5. State your claim 6 6. Pay the court costs 7 B. How can I get the other person to court? 7 1. Serving notice on the defendant 2. Alternative methods of serving notice on the defendant 8 3. Failed service of summons 4. Postponement of the trial C. What do I do if I’ve been sued in small claims court? 8 1. If you are being sued (someone else sued you first) 2. Counterclaims (someone filed a claim against you in response to your claim) 9 D. How should I prepare for trial? 11 1. Before court - preparing yourself 2. During court - proving your claim 12 3. After court - getting your money and appeals E. How do I appeal the judge’s decision? 12 IV. If I win, how do I get my money? 13 A. What happens to the losing party? B. Money: Garnishment 1. Garnishing wages 2. Garnishing a bank account 3. Executing your garnishment action (wages or bank account) 13 C. Other collection methods D. Satisfaction of judgment V. Terms commonly used in small claims court 15 TABLE OF CONTENTS I. INTRODUCTION TO SMALL CLAIMS COURT Small claims court is a division of the circuit court presided over by an appointed judge. Sm",
